{"id":"f753356251a9-0346","source":"references/pptset/【加赠】700页逻辑图形 (1).pptx","sourcePage":346,"slideXmlSha256":"cc8665be7e625c502c58c5c68c3285d9103690996c245f561430281b7c53d932","slots":[{"anchor":"s1010-s990-s989","text":"Paid value proposition","box":[0.4852,0.2392,0.1088,0.0568]},{"anchor":"s1010-s995-s994","text":"Free-to-use","box":[0.7942,0.254,0.1088,0.0322]},{"anchor":"s1010-s999","text":"Revenue streams","box":[0.6397,0.7145,0.1088,0.0322]},{"anchor":"s1010-s1004-s1003","text":"Pricing tactics","box":[0.5496,0.4843,0.1088,0.0322]},{"anchor":"s1010-s1009-s1008","text":"Third-party revenue generator","box":[0.7298,0.4722,0.1088,0.0568]},{"anchor":"s1013-s1011","text":"A revenue model is a framework for generating financial income. It identifies which revenue source to pursue, what value to offer, how to price the value, and who pays for the value. It is a key component of a company's business model. It primarily identifies what product or service will be created in order to generate revenues and the ways in which the product or service will be sold.\n\nWithout a clear and well-defined revenue model, with a clear plan of how to generate revenues, new businesses will more likely struggle due to costs which they will not be able to sustain. By having a clear revenue model, a business can focus on a target audience, fund development plans for a product or service, establish marketing plans, begin a line of credit and raise capital.","box":[0.0854,0.3564,0.3257,0.4843]},{"anchor":"s1013-s1012","text":"Revenue model choice framework","box":[0.0849,0.2195,0.277,0.1107]},{"anchor":"s2","text":"Revenue model choice framework","box":[0.0283,0.0378,0.9417,0.0673]}],"warnings":[],"stats":{"objects":34,"textBlocks":8},"reconstructedSlots":[{"anchor":"text-0","text":"Paid value ","box":[0.5101126945834058,0.24706590440538195,0.0624016016484416,0.020366668701171875],"origin":[0.5101126945834058,0.26335923936631944],"font":"DejaVuSans","size":10.998000144958496,"resolvedFami